# Document Extraction & Asset Management Enhancements

This plan addresses three core enhancements to the document extraction system:
1. **Inline Icon & Image Chunk Mapping**: Embedding textual representations of icons and images directly into chunk text streams and ensuring exact alignment between media items and their parent text paragraphs when chunks are split.
2. **First-Page Table Metadata Extraction & Deterministic Document IDs**: Extracting the `Document Name`, `Document Number`, and `Version` from first-page SOP tables before full extraction, using them to generate a deterministic `document_id`, and checking whether the document was previously uploaded.
3. **Per-Document Asset Management**: Storing extracted images and icons in dedicated per-document subdirectories (`data/extracted_images/{document_id}/` and `data/extracted_icons/{document_id}/`) so assets for each document are cleanly isolated and easy to view.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Deterministic Document ID Format**:
> The `document_id` will be generated by combining the extracted fields as `f"{clean_number}_{clean_name}_v{clean_version}"` (sanitizing special characters to alphanumeric, hyphens, and underscores). If any field cannot be extracted from the first page table, a safe fallback using the filename and default version (`1.0`) will be applied.

> [!NOTE]
> **Per-Document Asset Folders**:
> Currently, all images are stored flat in `data/extracted_images` and `data/extracted_icons`. With this change, each document will get its own folder:
> - `data/extracted_images/{document_id}/` for standard images
> - `data/extracted_icons/{document_id}/` for semantic icons
> When `IconExtractor` identifies an image as an icon, it will move the asset from the document's image directory into the document's icon directory.

> [!NOTE]
> **Inline Markers in Chunk Text**:
> `HierarchicalChunker` will inject inline markers such as `[Icon: warning | ID: ... | Path: ...]` or `[Image: caption | Path: ...]` into `chunk.content` at the exact reading order where the media appears in the AST. When `SemanticChunker` refines chunks into sub-chunks, it will filter `chunk.images` and `chunk.icons` so each sub-chunk only retains media items referenced in its portion of the text.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> **Duplicate Upload Handling Policy**:
> When a duplicate document upload is detected (i.e., a file with the same `(document_name, document_number, version)` already exists in `data/uploads/` or `data/output/`), our plan returns `already_uploaded: true` in the upload response and reuses the existing `document_id`. Should an optional `overwrite=true` query parameter be supported to force re-extraction if desired?

