### First-Page Metadata Extraction & ID Generation

#### [NEW] [metadata_extractor.py](file:///c:/Users/Bhavya/Desktop/Content%20Extraction/app/services/extraction/metadata_extractor.py)
- Implement `SOPMetadataExtractor` service with methods:
  - `extract_from_bytes(content: bytes, file_type: str, fallback_filename: str) -> tuple[str, str, str]`: Reads the first page of a PDF (using PyMuPDF/pdfplumber table detection) or DOCX (`doc.tables`) and scans for table rows matching `"Document Name"` / `"Title"`, `"Document Number"` / `"SOP Number"`, and `"Version"`. Includes a regex fallback on page 1 text headers.
  - `generate_document_id(doc_name: str, doc_number: str, doc_version: str, fallback_filename: str) -> str`: Generates a deterministic, sanitized `document_id`.
  - `check_duplicate_upload(document_id: str, settings: Settings) -> tuple[bool, bool]`: Returns `(already_uploaded, existing_output)` by checking `settings.upload_dir` and `settings.output_dir`.

#### [MODIFY] [upload.py](file:///c:/Users/Bhavya/Desktop/Content%20Extraction/app/api/upload.py)
- Update `UploadResponse` schema to include `already_uploaded: bool = False` and `existing_output: bool = False`.
- In `POST /documents/upload` and `POST /documents/upload/batch`:
  - Run `SOPMetadataExtractor.extract_from_bytes()` on the uploaded contents before saving.
  - Generate the deterministic `document_id` from the extracted metadata instead of a random UUID.
  - Check whether the document was previously uploaded. If already uploaded, set `already_uploaded = True` in the response while ensuring the file is stored at `settings.upload_dir / f"{document_id}{extension}"`.

#### [MODIFY] [pdf_parser.py](file:///c:/Users/Bhavya/Desktop/Content%20Extraction/app/services/parser/pdf_parser.py)
