### Text Chunking with Inline Icon/Image Mapping

#### [MODIFY] [hierarchical.py](file:///c:/Users/Bhavya/Desktop/Content%20Extraction/app/services/chunking/hierarchical.py)
- In `_traverse()`, when iterating over `node.children`:
  - For `IconNode`, append `f"[Icon: {child.semantic_meaning} | ID: {child.icon_id} | Path: {child.asset_path}]"` to `content_parts` so the media marker appears in reading order within `chunk.content`.
  - For `ImageNode`, append `f"[Image: {child.alt_text or 'image'} | Path: {child.asset_path}]"` to `content_parts`.
  - Ensure `chunk.icons` and `chunk.images` lists accurately track all icons/images in the chunk.

#### [MODIFY] [semantic.py](file:///c:/Users/Bhavya/Desktop/Content%20Extraction/app/services/chunking/semantic.py)
- When splitting a chunk into sub-chunks (`sub_chunks`):
  - Replace the logic that dumps all `tables`, `images`, and `icons` into the first sub-chunk (`idx == 0`).
  - Instead, check which icon/image paths or markers appear in `sub_content` and attach only those matching media items to each `sub_chunk.icons` and `sub_chunk.images`.

